<title>POLAND: POLISH NET RESERVES FALL TO $21.44 BLN IN FEB 1-10.</title>
<headline>POLISH NET RESERVES FALL TO $21.44 BLN IN FEB 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish net foreign currency</p>
<p>reserves fell by $29.5 million in February 1-10 to $21.44</p>
<p>billion and were $222.8 million lower than at the start of the</p>
<p>year, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dlrs)    FEB 1-10   JAN 97    FEB 96</p>
<p>    Official reserves		  NA	    NA	17.01</p>
<p>    Net reserves			21.44	 21.47    21.71</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves</p>
<p>are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount</p>
<p>of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
